[2026-09-20 12:38:32 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 087] --------------------------------------------------------------------------------
[2026-09-20 12:38:32 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 087]   Step 087 -- perturber distance ladder: what mass is required at
[2026-09-20 12:38:32 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 087]   any distance?
[2026-09-20 12:38:32 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 087]   Step 083 fixed the perturber's geometry to the published
[2026-09-20 12:38:32 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 087]   Brown & Batygin (2021) median location and showed the required mass
[2026-09-20 12:38:32 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 087]   is brown-dwarf scale (~4300 M_earth in-cap median).  That leaves one
[2026-09-20 12:38:32 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 087]   escape route: a perturber elsewhere -- closer, where a smaller mass
[2026-09-20 12:38:32 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 087]   delivers the same impulse, or farther, where surveys are shallower.
[2026-09-20 12:38:32 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 087]   This step closes it by measuring the required mass as a function of
[2026-09-20 12:38:32 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 087]   perturber semimajor axis, holding the anti-aligned shepherding
[2026-09-20 12:38:32 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 087]   geometry (e9 = 0.30, i9 = 15.6 deg, varpi9 = 246.7 deg, Om9 = 96.9
[2026-09-20 12:38:32 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 087]   deg, M9 = 180 deg residence-weighted) and the fiducial 6.9 M_earth
[2026-09-20 12:38:32 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 087]   mass.  Because the injected rotation scales linearly in mass
[2026-09-20 12:38:32 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 087]   (step 083, alpha = 1.00), a single rung at each distance yields the
[2026-09-20 12:38:32 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 087]   required mass directly:
[2026-09-20 12:38:32 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 087]   m_req(a9) = 6.9 * (d_of / drot_6.9(a9))
[2026-09-20 12:38:32 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 087]   Rungs: a9 = 250, 300, 461, 700, 1000 AU.  Deliverables: the
[2026-09-20 12:38:32 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 087]   required-mass distribution per rung in and out of the cap, the
[2026-09-20 12:38:32 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 087]   distance-scaling exponent gamma of m_req ~ a9^gamma, and the
[2026-09-20 12:38:32 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 087]   comparison against survey exclusion lines (IRAS/WISE all-sky limits
[2026-09-20 12:38:32 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 087]   of order Jupiter masses at these distances; BB21 nominal 5-10
[2026-09-20 12:38:32 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 087]   M_earth).  A point mass that must sit at any of these distances at
[2026-09-20 12:38:32 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 087]   ~10^3 M_earth is excluded by every relevant survey; a perturber
[2026-09-20 12:38:32 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 087]   closer still enters the planetary-ephemeris bounded regime.
